{"created": "2021-08-17T07:43:15.328337+00:00", "modified": "2024-07-18T20:48:17.851558+00:00", "id": 5166987, "conceptrecid": "5166986", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.5166986", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "metadata": {"title": "WikiChurches \u2013 A Fine-Grained Dataset of Architectural Styles with Real-World Challenges", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "publication_date": "2021-08-17", "description": "<p>WikiChurches is a dataset for architectural style classification, consisting of 9,485 images of church buildings. Both images and style labels were sourced from Wikipedia. The dataset can serve as a benchmark for various research fields, as it combines numerous real-world challenges: fine-grained distinctions between classes based on subtle visual features, a comparatively small sample size, a highly imbalanced class distribution, a high variance of viewpoints, and a hierarchical organization of labels, where only some images are labeled at the most precise level. In addition, we provide 631 bounding box annotations of characteristic visual features for 139 churches from four major categories. These annotations can, for example, be useful for research on fine-grained classification, where additional expert knowledge about distinctive object parts is often available.</p>\n\n<p>Please refer to the README.md file for information about the different files contained in this dataset.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bj\u00f6rn Barz", "affiliation": "Friedrich Schiller University Jena, Computer Vision Group", "orcid": "0000-0003-1019-9538"}, {"name": "Joachim Denzler", "affiliation": "Friedrich Schiller University Jena, Computer Vision Group", "orcid": "0000-0002-3193-3300"}], "keywords": ["Architectural Style Recognition", "Computer Vision", "Fine-Grained Visual Categorization", "Fine-Grained Visual Recognition", "Hierarchical Classification", "Class Hierarchy", "Data-efficient Deep Learning", "Imprecise Labels", "Imbalanced Classes"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.06959", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-sa-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "digitalarthistory"}, {"id": "computer-vision"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "5166986"}}]}, "notes": "<p>When using this dataset, please cite the following article:</p>\n<p>\nBj\u00f6rn Barz and Joachim Denzler.<br>\n\"WikiChurches: A Fine-Grained Dataset of Architectural Styles with Real-World Challenges.\"<br>\narXiv preprint arXiv:2108.06959, 2021.\n</p>"}, "title": "WikiChurches \u2013 A Fine-Grained Dataset of Architectural Styles with Real-World Challenges", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5166987", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5166987", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5166987?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5166987", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5166987/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5166986", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5166986", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5166986", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5166986", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5166987/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5166987/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5166987/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5166987/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5166987:datasheet.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5166987:data